WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.799
Given two partially overlapping images and a
keypoint in the first,

00:00:04.879 --> 00:00:07.414
where does its match land in the second?

00:00:07.494 --> 00:00:11.466
Local feature matching only answers when the point
is visible.

00:00:11.546 --> 00:00:14.211
But humans can also guess, or hallucinate,

00:00:14.291 --> 00:00:19.244
where an occluded or out of frame point should be,
using geometric reasoning.

00:00:19.324 --> 00:00:23.361
This paper, Visual Correspondence Hallucination
from ICLR 2022,

00:00:23.441 --> 00:00:29.048
trains a single network called NeurHal to output a
peaked probability distribution over

00:00:29.128 --> 00:00:32.381
the correspondent's location whether it is visible,

00:00:32.461 --> 00:00:34.930
occluded, or outside the field of view,

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:39.440
and shows this makes absolute camera pose
estimation far more robust.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:45.810
Establishing correspondences between two
overlapping images underlies much of computer vision,

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:48.135
from localization to reconstruction.

00:00:48.215 --> 00:00:53.883
But local feature matching only works when a
keypoint is actually visible in both images.

00:00:53.963 --> 00:00:56.143
When the correspondent is occluded,

00:00:56.223 --> 00:01:00.211
or when it falls outside the field of view of the
second image,

00:01:00.291 --> 00:01:05.378
these methods have nothing to say, and they simply
treat those regions as noise.

00:01:05.458 --> 00:01:09.640
So whenever two images share little overlap,
matching breaks down.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:12.766
Humans do not give up in these situations.

00:01:12.846 --> 00:01:15.794
Faced with an occluded or out of frame point,

00:01:15.874 --> 00:01:21.109
a person reasons about the geometry of the scene
and predicts, or hallucinates,

00:01:21.189 --> 00:01:22.859
where the match should be.

00:01:22.939 --> 00:01:27.636
Classical vision does use geometric reasoning, but
only after the fact,

00:01:27.716 --> 00:01:31.740
to filter out bad matches with models like epipolar
geometry.

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:37.527
No prior method actually predicts correspondences
at locations that are not covisible.

00:01:37.607 --> 00:01:40.420
That gap is exactly what this work targets.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:46.815
The paper introduces the task of visual
correspondence hallucination and a network to solve it,

00:01:46.895 --> 00:01:49.510
called NeurHal, for Neural Hallucinations.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:53.937
Given a pair of overlapping images and keypoints in
the source image,

00:01:54.017 --> 00:01:56.183
NeurHal outputs, for each keypoint,

00:01:56.263 --> 00:02:01.380
a probability distribution over its correspondent's
location in the target image,

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:06.063
whether that location is visible, occluded, or
outside the field of view.

00:02:06.143 --> 00:02:11.389
This unifies three tasks the authors name
identifying, inpainting, and outpainting.

00:02:11.469 --> 00:02:14.982
Because learning to hallucinate is unexplored territory,

00:02:15.062 --> 00:02:18.254
they first analyze what makes the task distinctive,

00:02:18.334 --> 00:02:22.360
and let that analysis drive the choice of loss and
architecture.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:24.301
Here is how NeurHal works.

00:02:24.381 --> 00:02:29.223
A siamese convolutional backbone turns both images
into dense descriptor maps.

00:02:29.303 --> 00:02:32.946
To allow correspondents outside the target's field
of view,

00:02:33.026 --> 00:02:36.038
the target map is padded with a learnable vector,

00:02:36.118 --> 00:02:39.193
initializing descriptors beyond the image borders.

00:02:39.273 --> 00:02:46.324
A cross attention backbone with positional encoding
then lets source and target descriptors exchange information,

00:02:46.404 --> 00:02:53.076
which is what enables the network to hallucinate
peaked distributions for occluded and out of frame points.

00:02:53.156 --> 00:02:58.503
Each keypoint's feature is convolved over the
target features and passed through a two

00:02:58.583 --> 00:03:01.153
D softmax to produce a correspondence map.

00:03:01.233 --> 00:03:04.939
Training minimizes a sum of Neural Reprojection
Error terms,

00:03:05.019 --> 00:03:08.789
the negative log likelihood of the true reprojected
location,

00:03:08.869 --> 00:03:13.900
with no covisibility assumption and no need to
label points as visible or hidden.

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:18.480
The method is evaluated across both indoor and
outdoor domains.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:23.915
Indoors, NeurHal is trained on ScanNet and also
tested on the NYU Depth dataset;

00:03:23.995 --> 00:03:28.195
outdoors, it is trained on MegaDepth and tested on
ETH three D.

00:03:28.275 --> 00:03:33.426
Crucially, every evaluation uses scenes that were
never seen during training,

00:03:33.506 --> 00:03:36.552
so the results measure genuine generalization.

00:03:36.632 --> 00:03:38.658
For the downstream application,

00:03:38.738 --> 00:03:44.772
absolute camera pose estimation is measured on
twenty five hundred source and target image

00:03:44.852 --> 00:03:47.150
pairs from held out ScanNet scenes.

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:50.529
The experiments confirm both research questions.

00:03:50.609 --> 00:03:56.237
NeurHal successfully hallucinates correspondences
on scenes it never saw during training,

00:03:56.317 --> 00:04:02.330
for occluded points that must be inpainted and for
out of frame points that must be outpainted,

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:07.397
with prediction errors concentrated well below what
random guessing would give.

00:04:07.477 --> 00:04:10.860
State of the art matching methods like LoFTR, DRC Net,

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:15.927
and S two D Net do poorly on inpainting and
essentially cannot outpaint at all,

00:04:16.007 --> 00:04:19.518
since they only ever search inside the image boundaries.

00:04:19.598 --> 00:04:22.020
And on absolute camera pose estimation,

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:26.830
NeurHal is correct far more often than any
competitor on low overlap pairs,

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:30.550
precisely because it is the only method that can outpaint.

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:35.944
An ablation on ScanNet isolates what each task
contributes to pose robustness.

00:04:36.024 --> 00:04:40.712
Training NeurHal on all three tasks together,
identification, inpainting,

00:04:40.792 --> 00:04:43.325
and outpainting, gives the best results.

00:04:43.405 --> 00:04:50.118
The key finding is that adding the outpainting task
is what drives the improvement on low overlap pairs,

00:04:50.198 --> 00:04:54.428
where most correspondents fall outside the target's
field of view.

00:04:54.508 --> 00:04:56.453
Adding inpainting, by contrast,

00:04:56.533 --> 00:05:00.306
brings little additional benefit to camera pose
estimation.

00:05:00.386 --> 00:05:06.119
Here a pose counts as correct when rotation error
is under twenty degrees and translation

00:05:06.199 --> 00:05:08.340
error under one point five meters.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:10.616
A few numbers anchor the setup.

00:05:10.696 --> 00:05:16.737
Pose estimates are judged correct under a rotation
threshold of twenty degrees and a translation

00:05:16.817 --> 00:05:18.968
threshold of one point five meters,

00:05:19.048 --> 00:05:22.985
measured over twenty five hundred held out ScanNet
image pairs.

00:05:23.065 --> 00:05:27.129
NeurHal produces deliberately low resolution
correspondence maps,

00:05:27.209 --> 00:05:31.719
using an effective stride of eight and an output
ratio of fifty percent,

00:05:31.799 --> 00:05:38.477
so a six hundred forty by four hundred eighty
target yields a one hundred sixty by one hundred twenty map.

00:05:38.557 --> 00:05:43.322
And across all the methods tested, NeurHal is the
only one able to outpaint,

00:05:43.402 --> 00:05:47.020
to place correspondents beyond the target image's borders.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:49.628
The takeaway is simple but powerful.

00:05:49.708 --> 00:05:55.782
A single network can learn to hallucinate keypoint
correspondences whether the match is visible,

00:05:55.862 --> 00:05:58.859
occluded, or entirely outside the field of view,

00:05:58.939 --> 00:06:05.206
and this ability makes absolute camera pose
estimation much more robust when images barely overlap.

00:06:05.286 --> 00:06:10.399
In effect, NeurHal reframes non covisible regions
not as noise to be thrown away,

00:06:10.479 --> 00:06:14.630
but as signal to be predicted through learned
geometric reasoning.
